{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for journal-floor draft 4 at exact 149e50cef2e3363f72daff3baf8f8187261d9e58, tree 13264b26ef3fb574e5b22ef44d155745e211b5be. Primary 033cc854 was read first in full (664 lines), and the complete delta from draft 3 was reviewed. One remaining finding.\n\n[P2] Specify a bounded lookup from a retained key to its owning pass. The new layout makes a file's path depend on the first pass that wrote it (section 2.2:96–110), and writer rule 6 requires a later use to name that earlier pass without writing a second copy (:126–128). But the new input gives the key (kind/domain/digest), not the old pass number. Neither the proposed layout nor the writer rules name an index or another bounded way to obtain that number or prove the key has never been archived. The existing ArchiveRow has confirmed commit/through plus one pending manifest, not a retained-key directory (archive-row.ts:23–33); the native retained tables also carry no archive-pass locator (sqlite.ts:105–106).\n\nAfter 10,000 passes and a restart, let a new entry reuse a key first written in an arbitrary nonrecent pass. Its digest and the opaque confirmed commit do not identify that pass directory. Searching the per-pass files or manifests can read one tree/manifest per old pass, contrary to rule 7's history-independent charged cost; treating a failed bounded search as absence creates the duplicate that rule 6 forbids. The extended witness currently adds new keys only, so it does not test this lookup. Define a durable bounded key-to-owner lookup tied to the confirmed archive basis, including how confirmation, restart and v1 conversion maintain it and how reads/updates are charged; alternatively use a stable key-addressed layout that needs no owner lookup. Extend the existing tree-work witness with a nonrecent reused key and a genuinely new key after restart, asserting bounded discovery work as well as no duplicate or relocated file. This is a design gap in the new per-pass remedy, not an observed implementation failure.\n\nAll three earlier fc12d8e0 findings are addressed by the written changes. Completed OwnRequest rows explicitly remain lifetime state, with the sending hash copied before origin deletion, held-entry/request-row hash selection, unchanged lookup/export semantics and a two-floor/restart/checkpoint witness. Per-pass retained paths now stay stable, reject wrong owners and move v1 retained files into pass 0's directory; the v1 complete-name-set relocation rule is explicitly excluded. Four three-digit levels bound the numeric directories and the writer/reader share an explicit maximum of 999,999,999,999. The new lookup issue above must be resolved before the retained-layout cost guarantee is complete.\n\nThe delta is confined to these request-row and layout corrections, their citations, corresponding effect/state-digest text, witnesses and renumbering. All 2,569 other tracked paths remain unchanged from draft 3 and the declared baseline 7a148325. Nine exact baseline source files were preserved and inspected for request snapshots, original archive receipt/row state, retained table schemas, v1 physical layout and bounds. The cited source supports the proposed request-row correction. Static path/information examples are recorded; no floor/v2 program, archive operation or software test was executed.\n\nNative Source 033cc854 is effective/current at exact head/path and directly cites bb6edf4a, with the live f9fcee34 commitment. Native prepare assigns that implementation. Planner survey 2376ac41 naming draft 4 was read in full and considered. Documentation-only whitespace check passed (exit 0); no project tests or gate were run. Trees: draft 3 4fb38ccabfbc77cfca4c87048651b905ae534ce4; draft 4 13264b26ef3fb574e5b22ef44d155745e211b5be; baseline 4b5a2fa12d92c083ddcdd1ffd61fbd15d090969b. No implementation, source/ref mutation, installation, merge, push, provider or deployment action.\n\nClosed evidence /private/tmp/checker-floor-d4-i9hlnwsj: 16 regular leaves; CLOSED-MANIFEST.json 3,105 bytes, SHA-256 138954af290e4c8d7662fd857f499286374d6a3cf05c2924b1468b33e008afc3. Entire root permanently frozen forever; read/stable-copy only. The first guarded submission refused an extraneous acknowledgment of the survey's abbreviated head; no verdict was recorded by it. This submission uses the required empty exact-head-news set.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:033cc854dcf5538b9e161f7483280369f80913a3","binding":"assigned","head":"149e50cef2e3363f72daff3baf8f8187261d9e58","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8e3c70821d15e9533fe351891442c3856cbe12e4\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bb6edf4ab388a0a05bf5332890c734868be73acf\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f12018c856f2b6187c0bc87fcbc7d400d9520342","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}